FIXED!

I imagined that A.constr <- list(A = as.matrix(t(Q)%*%A), e = rep(0,n.covariates)) should be defined across the entire A projection matrix for the spatio-temporal process and then apply parts of the A.constr to each timepoint accordingly through the group indicator.

Since the constraints that I wish to apply are the same across each time point separately in fact what I should have done is define a new projection matrix Au <- inla.spde.make.A(mesh, loc = as.matrix(xmat[, c("x", "y")])) for only one time point.

